  "body": " Cows and Goats   In a village survey of households, keep cows, keep goats and keep neither.     Let households keep both. Write the number in each of the four regions in terms of .  Cows only ; both ; goats only ; neither .    The four regions hold all households. Write an equation and solve it.  , so and .    How many households keep cows only? Goats only?  Cows only ; goats only .    Combine the class's data from home (on paper or in a spreadsheet) and draw the Venn diagram.  Answers depend on the class. Check that the four regions add up to the number of homes surveyed.      "
