  "body": " Reflect, Then Rotate   A sign painter in Kakamega copies a triangle with vertices , and onto a board twice. is the reflection in the -axis and is the rotation of anticlockwise about :      Find the image of the triangle under . Draw both triangles.  , , .    Find the image of under . Draw it.  , , . See .    Work out the product . Use it on , and . Do you get the same final image?  , which sends , , to , , : the same final image.    Now work out and use it on , and . Is the final image the same as before?  , giving , , . This is a different image.    Use the table of standard matrices to name the single transformations and .  is the reflection in the line ; is the reflection in the line . They are different, so the order matters.  Learners who did first and then have used the matrix . Let them check part (d) against their drawing.      "
