  "body": " Undoing Two Transformations   A point is transformed by , and its image is then reflected in the line (matrix ). The final image is . Find the matrix that undoes both transformations, and the original point.    Method 1: invert the single matrix.  is done first, so the single matrix is Its determinant is , so .  Method 2: undo the last one first.  is its own inverse, and . Undo first, then : the same matrix.  The original point is . Check: .   "
