  "title": "Challenge: A Matrix That Undoes Itself.",
  "body": " Challenge: A Matrix That Undoes Itself  Show that is its own inverse. What happens to a point that is transformed by this matrix twice?  Work out the square of the matrix.  Its square is ; the point returns to where it started.  . So the matrix times itself is , which means it is its own inverse: the second transformation undoes the first and the point returns to its start.  "
