  "body": " (solid) and (dashed) for .   Both waves cross the x-axis at 0, 180 and 360 degrees; y = sin x reaches 1 and -1, y = 2 sin x reaches 2 and -2.  Both curves start at 0. The solid curve y = sin x rises to 1 at 90 degrees, falls to -1 at 270 degrees and returns to 0 at 360 degrees. The dashed curve y = 2 sin x does the same with greatest value 2 and least value -2.    "
