  "body": " Column Vectors in Terms of Unit Vectors       Strand  2.0 Measurements and Geometry    Sub-Strand  2.6 Vectors II    Specific Learning Outcomes  Express column and position vectors in terms of unit vectors in different situations    Grade Level  12    Estimated Duration  40 minutes         Upon completion of this lesson, learners will be able to:  Know: the unit vectors , , ; a column is ; vectors are added, subtracted and multiplied by scalars component by component.  Do: change a vector from one form to the other; add, subtract and multiply vectors by scalars in either form; solve simple vector equations.  Apply: combine two displacements of a drone into one.     Problem-Solving and Discovery   Suggested Time 14 minutes  Objective Learners see that , and are building blocks for every vector, and that operations work component by component.  Teacher's Role Work in pairs: one learner writes each answer as a column, the other in , , form. Swap roles at part (d). Ask after part (d): Where did the go?     From Columns to , , and Back   Let , and .     Draw , and on a sketch of the three axes.  Each is an arrow of length from : along , along , along .    Write , and as multiples of , or .  , , .    Add the three columns in (b). Write the result as a column and in terms of , and .  .    Write as a column.  . There is no term, so the middle component is .    and . Find in both forms.  .    Find .  and , so .        Structured Instruction    Suggested Time 8 minutes  Objective To formalise the unit vectors , , and the operations on vectors in three dimensions.     Key Takeaways & Teacher Connection   Connecting to Learner Work: parts (c) and (d) wrote the same vector in two ways.  A zero component is left out of , , form but kept as in a column.  Parts (e) and (f): add or subtract matching components; a scalar multiplies every component.      Unit Vectors , and  A unit vector is a vector of magnitude . The unit vectors along the axes , and are Each is one step along an axis. Every vector can be built from them: A zero component is left out ( ), and a coefficient is not written ( , not ). The point has position vector .    Operations in Three Dimensions  To add or subtract vectors, add or subtract matching components. To multiply a vector by a number (a scalar ), multiply every component by : In , , form, collect the terms, the terms and the terms. A scalar multiplies every component; it never adds to them.  The zero vector  has every component ; .    The unit vectors , , , and built from , and .   Short thick arrows i, j and k along the x-, y- and z-axes. Arrows 2i, then minus 3j, then 4k are placed tip to tail and reach the point (2, minus 3, 4); a dashed arrow goes straight from O to that point.      Vectors in a Spreadsheet  A spreadsheet does vector arithmetic one column at a time. Put the headings x , y , z in cells B1 to D1 , the components of in row 2 and those of in row 3. In B4 type =2*B2-3*B3 and fill it right to D4 : row 4 is . In E2 , =SQRT(SUMSQ(B2:D2)) gives the magnitude of , which you meet in . Change a component and every result updates.    Practice and Application     Suggested Time  10 minutes    Objective  To apply the learned concepts and procedures to solve varied problems.    Teacher's Role  The teacher works through the following examples with the class, asking questions and connecting to insights from the learner experience.       Changing the Form   (a) Write in terms of , and . (b) Write as a column. (c) Write the position vector of in terms of , and .    (a) : the component is , so it is left out.  (b) There is no term, so the middle component is : .  (c) .     Adding and Subtracting in Three Dimensions   and . Find , and .    and .  Multiply first, then add:     Unknown Constants   and , and . Find , and .    . Equal vectors have equal components, so     Assessment \/ Evaluate     Suggested Time  8 minutes    Objective  To formatively assess individual Learner understanding of the lesson objectives.    Learning Experience  Learners independently complete a short assessment task (select from the exercises below).    Teacher's Role  Collect and review the exit tickets to gauge Learner understanding and identify any common misconceptions that need to be addressed in the next lesson.       Checkpoint Guide   Teacher's Role      Pair Learners strategically so stronger learners can explain reasoning to peers.    Collect and review the exit tickets to gauge Learner understanding and identify any common misconceptions that need to be addressed in the next lesson.      Instructions to Give Leaners      Click Show new example question to load the problem    Solve the displayed question    Click Submit to check your answer    If incorrect, carefully read the feedback and analyse the error before trying a new question. The immediate feedback from checkpoint submissions allows Learners to identify and correct errors in real-time.    Complete at least 5 questions before rotating      Type one number in each box of a column vector. Fractions may be typed with a slash, for example 5\/2 . Type vectors in , , form like 3i-2j+5k ; leave out a zero component.                Write in terms of , and : (a) (b)  (a) (b)    Write as columns: (a) (b)  (a) (b)    and . Find (a) (b) (c) .  (a) (b) (c)    A drone over a shamba near Nakuru makes the displacement and then , in metres. What single displacement has the same effect?  metres    Find the vector if .   , so .    Challenge: Building a Vector from Two Others  and .  Find numbers and with .  Show that no numbers and give .    Use two components to find and , then test the third.  (a) , (b) the first two components force , , which give a third component of , not .  (a) The first two components give and . From the first, ; then , so and . Check the third: . Correct.  (b) The first two components are the same equations, so again , . But then the third component is , not . No and work.     Differentiation   Differentiation Strategies   Learner Group Strategy and Learning Experience  Struggling Learners (Support) Give a three-row grid with rows labelled , , to fill in component by component. Focus on activity parts (a) to (d) and . Assign and .  On-Level Learners (Core) Full activity plus all examples. Assign to .  Advanced Learners (Challenge) All exercises including . Extension: find the vector with for , in . (Answer: .)      Assessment   Assessment methods    Type  Method  Purpose    Formative (During Lesson)   Observation: Teacher circulates during the anchor task, listening to group discussions.  Questioning: Teacher asks probing questions to check for understanding.  Exit Ticket: A short, independent task at the end of the lesson.    To monitor learner progress in real-time, provide immediate feedback, and adjust instruction as needed.     Summative (After Lesson)   Homework assignment with more complex problems.  Future quiz\/test questions.    To evaluate mastery of the learning objectives after instruction and practice.        Teacher Reflection  Complete this after the lesson   What went well?    What would I change?    Learner Understanding: What did the exit tickets reveal about Learner learning?    Next Steps: Based on the assessment data, what is the plan for the next lesson?      "
