  "body": " The Midpoint Theorem   Draw any triangle and let and . Mark , the midpoint of , and , the midpoint of .   Triangle with and the midpoints of and .   Triangle OAB with arrow a from O to A and arrow b from O to B. M is the midpoint of OA and N the midpoint of OB. The segment MN is parallel to AB and half as long.        Write and in terms of and .  , .    Find .  .    Find .  .    What do (b) and (c) tell you about the lines and ?  : is parallel to and half as long.    Measure and in your own triangle. Does your drawing agree?  Every triangle gives , up to measuring error, with parallel to .    Now let and be one third of the way from to and from to . What is ?  : parallel to and a third as long.      "
